+# Summary: range matching (`satisfies`, `max_satisfying`)
+
+## What changed
+
+- `depres/ranges.py`: replaced the two `NotImplementedError` stubs with an implementation of the contract in `docs/RANGES.md`:
+  - Parses ranges into `||` unions of comparator sets; whitespace between operator and version is allowed; the empty set matches everything.
+  - Handles primitives, partial versions and X-ranges, hyphen ranges, tilde and caret ranges, with the partial-version rules from the doc.
+  - Applies the prerelease rule per comparator set: a prerelease version matches only if a comparator in the same set names the same `major.minor.patch` with a prerelease tag.
+  - `satisfies` and `max_satisfying` raise `ValueError` for invalid ranges and invalid versions. `max_satisfying` returns the input element unchanged, or `None`.
+- `tests/test_ranges_contract.py` (new): 22 tests (the suite totals 30 with the 8 existing ones), covering each example in `docs/RANGES.md`, invalid inputs, and `max_satisfying` behaviour.
+- `tests/test_ranges.py` and `depres/version.py`: not changed.
+- This file (`SUMMARY.md`) is new.
+
+## What I verified
+
+- `python -m unittest` (Python 3.14.3, run from the project root): before the change, all 8 tests in `tests/test_ranges.py` errored. After it: `Ran 30 tests ... OK`.
+- One of my new tests failed on the first run because I had written it wrong: `1.2.3-2.3` without spaces is a valid prerelease version, not a hyphen range. I corrected the test to match the spec. I did not change the implementation for it.
+- Spot checks: `>=1.2.3-alpha <2` matches `1.2.3-beta`; `*` does not match `0.0.0-alpha`; `>*` matches nothing.
+
+## Not verified / uncertain
+
+- No CI config exists in this checkout (no `.github/` or similar), so I could not confirm CI's Python version or flags. I only ran the suite locally on 3.14.3.
+- I did not compare against the real npm `semver` package. Behaviour for cases the doc does not cover is my choice, and may differ from npm:
+  - `>*` and `<*` match nothing; `>=*`, `<=*` and `=*` match everything.
+  - `^0.0.0` means `<0.0.1`.
+  - A leading `v` is accepted after an operator (`>=v1.2.3`).
+  - Build metadata is accepted and ignored in ranges.
+  - A prerelease in a hyphen bound counts for the prerelease rule, as in npm.
+  - Prerelease tags are not allowed on partial versions (`1.2-beta` is invalid).
+- The lockfile checker that the doc mentions was not in scope and I did not touch it.
+- Nothing has been committed.
